1. Definitions and scope

"Copyright Holder" means the person or entity entitled to license the applicable
Cadence material. This license covers only material that the Copyright Holder
has the right to license. Third-party materials remain under their own licenses.

"Software" means the Cadence Agent Skill, instructions, design-system
documentation, reusable components, themes, style packs, templates, scripts,
and accompanying source code and assets, to the extent owned or licensable by
the Copyright Holder. It does not include independently licensed third-party
material or the user's data and independently authored report content.

"Modified Version" means a copy or derivative of the Software made by changing,
translating, adapting, renaming, or repackaging its protected material. Merely
using Cadence to generate a report does not make that report a Modified Version
for purposes of the resale restriction.

"Outputs" means reports, HTML pages, visualizations, analyses, and other
deliverables created using the Software for readers or clients. An Output may
contain Software components needed to display, interact with, or distribute
that deliverable. A reusable Skill, component library, theme or template pack,
plugin, or repackaged Cadence product offered as software is not an Output
merely because it was generated with Cadence or called a report.

"Resale" means distributing or licensing the Software or a Modified Version
as a standalone paid software product, in exchange for payment or other
consideration for the software copy or license. This includes selling Cadence
itself and selling renamed or repackaged versions as paid Skills, template
packs, component packs, themes, or plugins. Charging for Outputs or Commercial
Services as permitted below is not, by itself, Resale.

"Commercial Services" means paid analysis, research, report creation,
customization, consulting, training, maintenance, or technical support using
the Software, where the service or Output is the deliverable rather than a
standalone paid license or copy of the Software.

2. Free permission

Subject to these terms, permission is granted, without license fees, to any
individual or organization to use, study, copy, fork, and modify the Software
and to distribute original or Modified Versions without charging for the
software copy or license. Personal, educational, research, and internal
commercial use are expressly permitted. Ordinary enterprise use does not
require separate commercial authorization or a paid license.

When distributing Software or Modified Versions, retain this license and
applicable copyright, attribution, and third-party license notices. Recipients
must receive these terms for the covered Software; renaming or modifying it
does not remove the resale restriction on that material. No source publication
obligation is imposed by this license. Third-party obligations remain separate.

3. Outputs and Commercial Services

You may create, use, sell, license, and deliver Outputs, including commercial
analytical reports and interactive HTML reports, and charge clients for
Commercial Services. You may choose the terms for your own report content and
data to the extent you have rights in them. The resale restriction does not
automatically apply to Outputs or their content, and no Cadence royalty or
separate commercial authorization is required solely for such activity.

Software embedded in an Output for that Output's rendering or interaction may
be delivered with the paid Output under this permission. Retain applicable
Software and third-party notices, which may be in source comments, metadata,
or accompanying files rather than a visible report badge. This exception does
not authorize marketing the embedded Software as a separate paid reusable
software product. No rights in client data or third-party content are granted.

4. Restriction on Resale and separate authorization

Without prior written authorization from the Copyright Holder, you may not
engage in Resale of the Software or a Modified Version. Modifying, renaming,
or repackaging the Software does not avoid this restriction.

The Copyright Holder may grant separate written permission for commercial
software distribution on terms agreed with the recipient. Such permission
does not relicense third-party material or remove its obligations.

5. Boundary cases

This draft does not establish an additional blanket prohibition or paid-license
requirement for paid SaaS hosting, mixed software bundles, membership downloads,
or deliveries charging only technical-service fees. Their classification
depends on whether the actual transaction is the standalone software Resale
defined above or permitted use, Outputs, or Commercial Services. Ordinary
report services remain expressly permitted. Unresolved cases are identified
for owner and legal review in docs/licensing-review.md; recommendations there
are not additional license restrictions.

6. Third parties and names

Separate licenses govern third-party code, fonts, and other materials, including
the bundled SIL Open Font License fonts. Nothing in this license limits rights
granted by those licenses or asserts ownership of third-party material. This
license grants no trademark rights or permission to imply endorsement.

